  "id": "meissners-corpuscle",
  "term": "Meissner’s corpuscle",
  "definition": "Meissner’s corpuscle is a small oval structure in the skin’s papillae, especially in the fingers and toes. It is a touch receptor made of a connective tissue capsule containing nerve endings around wedge-shaped epithelioid cells.",
